@*
    Audit Configuration workspace (537, 2026-11-13; 543 the same day).

    Screen key : `org-audit-configuration`
    Group      : Audit Management

    REQUEST (sir, 537): the page showed two Organization pickers -- the flow
    shell's context bar and each hosted screen's own. Make it a list of
    the audits to configure; a row click opens the audit's view.

    REQUEST (sir, 543): Scope Builder and Question Sets move here from Audit
    Definition (which keeps only the audit details). Each step opens on its
    own (follow-up: in a row under the step) and is saved there; once
    saved, the step shows Completed. Submit for Review and Approve live here (542, folded in).

    MODES, ONE PAGE (the Audit Definition workspace pattern)
      list  -- every Draft and Under Review audit of the organization
               (sp_org_assurance_configuration_list,
               GET /org-assurance/configuration-audits; Under Review first).
               One Organization picker. Columns: Code, Name, Owner, Version,
               Status (Draft / Under Review) and Configured (n/4; 548) -- no
               per-step columns (sir).
               3-dot: View, and Submit for Review (Draft) / Approve
               (Under Review).
      view  -- row click / View: the audit's facts and its six steps
               (GET definitions/{id} + setup-status). A step's Configure
               button opens its screen under the row. Submit for Review
               (Draft, enabled once every step is Completed) and Approve (Under Review) sit under
               the steps and on Actions.
      Opened from Audit Definition's "Audit Configuration" item, the page
      reads the audit from the encrypted navigation code (?code=,
      Shared/secure-nav.js) and opens its view.
      No record id is written to the address bar; the mode lives in the
      page (standing rule: no plain ids in a URL).

    STEP ROWS EXPAND (543; sir, same day: instead of popups and the Scope
    Builder full page -- the Question Sets grid's expand pattern)
      The step list has a Configure column: one button (pen) per step. It opens
      that step's screen in a row right under the step (one step open at
      a time); pressing it again, or Cancel, closes it. A row click does
      nothing. The flow shell (Partials/_audit-flow-shell, hosted mode)
      waits in a hidden holder with every step's panel; opening a step
      moves its panel into a frame (caption, panel, Cancel / Save) and the
      frame into the expand row; closing moves both back. The open step's
      row stays highlighted, and the page does not scroll -- the step opens
      downward from where it was clicked. The hosted
      screens are unchanged apart from the reload hooks below.
        Scope Builder  save window.__oaScopeBuilder.save()    -> bool
        Question Sets  save window.__oaAdoption.save()        -> bool
        Workflow       save window.__oaWorkflowConfig.save()  -> bool
        Scoring        save window.__oaScoringConfig.save()   -> bool
        548: Trigger is no longer a step. 545: Scope Resolution is no longer a step (the scope is
        resolved when an execution is created); its screen is the Preview
        under the Scope Builder (Partials/_audit-scope-step).
      Save closes the step and re-reads the step list (its chip turns
      Completed). Every open re-reads the step (its reload(), quiet), so
      edits thrown away by closing unsaved are not shown next time; closing
      after a change (Cancel, the button again, another step, Back) asks
      first. A failed Save keeps the step open with the screen's own
      message in it. The step list re-renders on refresh; an open step is
      put back under its row (mountFrame).

    WHY DRAFT ONLY
      Every step saves only while the version is Draft (074, 084, 087, 093,
      277). Under Review (and any other status) a step opens read-only (its
      button reads View): the hosted screens show their own read-only line
      and there is no Save. Submit for Review requires every step (537 gate, THROW 53612).

    REUSE
      The six step screens are hosted unchanged through the flow shell;
      chips come from the shell (window.__oaFlowShell.chipHtml); the row
      and page Actions menus are js/Shared/page-actions-menu.js; the facts
      layout is the Audit Definition view's (.oa-ws-view); message boxes
      are gracUi.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.AuditFlowShell

<partial name="Partials/_workflow-common" />

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Screen.Group / @Model.Screen.Title</p>
        <h1 id="oaCfgHeading">@Model.Screen.Title</h1>
        <p id="oaCfgSubtitle">@Model.Screen.Description</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pm-actions">
        <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="oaCfgActionsBtn" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" hidden>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-bolt" aria-hidden="true"></i> Actions
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:10px; margin-left:2px;"></i>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="oaCfgBack" hidden>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true"></i> <span id="oaCfgBackLabel">Back to audit list</span>
        </button>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="oa-cfg" id="oaCfgRoot" data-mode="list">

    @* ---------------- List ---------------- *@
    <section class="pm-panel oa-cfg-list">
        <div class="pm-toolbar">
            <select id="oaCfgFilterOrganization" aria-label="Organization"><option value="">Loading organizations...</option></select>
            <input id="oaCfgSearch" type="text" placeholder="Search name / code..." />
            <button class="pm-button icon" id="oaCfgRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
        <p class="oa-ws-section-hint">Draft audits are configured here, one step at a time; once every step is complete, submit the audit for review. Audits under review are approved here.</p>
        <div class="pm-table-wrap">
            <table>
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        @* 543 follow-up (sir): no per-step columns -- Configured
                           (n/6) and the audit's Status say enough here; the
                           steps are on the audit's view. *@
                        <th>Code</th><th>Name</th><th>Owner</th><th>Version</th><th>Status</th>
                        <th>Configured</th><th>Actions</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="oaCfgBody">
                    <tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">Select an organization to load audits.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-pager" data-pager="oa-cfg">
            <button class="pm-button" data-pg="prev" type="button">Previous</button>
            <span data-pg="label">Page 1</span>
            <button class="pm-button" data-pg="next" type="button">Next</button>
            <span data-pg="total" class="pm-pager-total">0 total</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ---------------- View: facts, and the steps (Configure opens a step under its row) ---------------- *@
    <section class="pm-panel oa-ws-view">
        <div class="pm-toolbar" style="justify-content:space-between">
            <div style="display:flex; gap:6px; align-items:center;">
                <span class="pm-badge" id="oaCfgStatus">-</span>
                <span class="pm-badge" id="oaCfgVersion" hidden></span>
            </div>
            <button class="pm-button icon" id="oaCfgViewRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-message" id="oaCfgMessage" style="display:none;"></div>

        <h3 class="oa-wv-section">Audit</h3>
        <dl class="oa-wv-facts" id="oaCfgFacts"></dl>

        <h3 class="oa-wv-section">Configuration</h3>
        <div class="pm-table-wrap oa-cfg-steps-wrap">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Status</th><th>Items</th><th>Configure</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody id="oaCfgSteps"></tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        @* 542 / 543: review from here. Submit is enabled once every step
           is Completed; Approve shows while the audit is Under Review. *@
        <div class="oa-flow-nav oa-cfg-savebar">
            <span class="oa-ws-section-hint" id="oaCfgReady"></span>
            <span style="display:flex; gap:8px;">
                <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="oaCfgSubmit" hidden>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-paper-plane" aria-hidden="true"></i> Submit for Review
                </button>
                <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="oaCfgApprove" hidden>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Approve
                </button>
            </span>
        </div>
    </section>

    @* ---------------- Audit view (sir, 2026-11-13) ----------------
       The list's 3-dot "View": the Audit Definition view page -- the whole
       audit, configuration included, read-only (js/Shared/audit-view.js).
       A row click still opens the step list above. *@
    <section class="pm-panel oa-ws-view oa-cfg-audit">
        <div class="pm-toolbar" style="justify-content:space-between">
            <div style="display:flex; gap:6px; align-items:center;">
                <span class="pm-badge" id="oaCfgAvStatus">-</span>
                <span class="pm-badge" id="oaCfgAvVersion" hidden></span>
            </div>
            <button class="pm-button icon" id="oaCfgAvRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-message" id="oaCfgAvMessage" style="display:none;"></div>
        <div id="oaCfgAvBody"></div>
    </section>

    @* ---------------- Step screens (543) ----------------
       The flow shell, hosted, waits here hidden with every step's panel,
       and so does the frame an open step is shown in (caption, the panel,
       Cancel / Save). The Configure button of a step row moves the frame,
       with that step's panel in it, into a row under the step; closing
       moves both back. The flag is set before the hosted screens' scripts
       run: they then leave the address bar alone (no ?definitionId=). *@
    <div id="oaCfgHolder" hidden>
        <script>window.__oaHostNoUrl = true;</script>
        <partial name="Partials/_audit-flow-shell" model="Model" />
        <div class="oa-cfg-frame" id="oaCfgFrame">
            <p class="oa-ws-section-hint" id="oaCfgFrameCaption"></p>
            <div id="oaCfgFrameBody"></div>
            <div class="oa-flow-nav oa-cfg-savebar">
                <span class="oa-ws-section-hint" id="oaCfgFrameHint"></span>
                <span style="display:flex; gap:8px;">
                    <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="oaCfgFrameCancel">Cancel</button>
                    <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="oaCfgFrameSave">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk" aria-hidden="true"></i> Save
                    </button>
                </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<script src="~/js/Shared/page-actions-menu.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script src="~/js/Shared/secure-nav.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script src="~/js/Shared/audit-view.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script>
(function () {
    'use strict';

    const root = document.getElementById('oaCfgRoot');
    const wf   = window.__wfCommon;
    if (!root || !wf) return;

    const API = '/practice/api/org-assurance';
    const U   = p => String(window.appBasePath || window.pmPathBase || '').replace(/\/+$/, '') + p;
    const esc = wf.escape;
    const pick = function (o, a, b) { return o ? (o[a] != null ? o[a] : o[b]) : null; };

    const state = {
        mode: 'list', orgId: '', definitionId: '', name: '', statusCode: '',
        steps: [], rows: {},
        search: '', page: 1, pageSize: 25, total: 0
    };

    const el = {
        heading  : document.getElementById('oaCfgHeading'),
        subtitle : document.getElementById('oaCfgSubtitle'),
        actions  : document.getElementById('oaCfgActionsBtn'),
        back     : document.getElementById('oaCfgBack'),
        backText : document.getElementById('oaCfgBackLabel'),
        body     : document.getElementById('oaCfgBody'),
        org      : document.getElementById('oaCfgFilterOrganization'),
        submit   : document.getElementById('oaCfgSubmit'),
        approve  : document.getElementById('oaCfgApprove'),
        holder   : document.getElementById('oaCfgHolder')
    };

    function chip(status) {
        const shell = window.__oaFlowShell;
        return shell ? shell.chipHtml(status || 'NotConfigured') : esc(status || '');
    }
    function box(message, type) {
        if (window.gracUi) return window.gracUi.alert(message, { type: type });
        window.alert(message);
        return Promise.resolve();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Mode
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function setMode(mode) {
        state.mode = mode;
        root.setAttribute('data-mode', mode);
        el.actions.hidden = mode !== 'view' && mode !== 'audit';
        el.back.hidden = mode === 'list';
        el.backText.textContent = 'Back to audit list';
        if (mode === 'list') {
            el.heading.textContent  = 'Audit Configuration';
            el.subtitle.textContent = 'Draft and Under Review audits: scope, question sets, workflow and scoring.';
        }
        window.scrollTo(0, 0);
    }

    el.back.addEventListener('click', async function () {
        // An open step closes first (asking when it has changes).
        if (!(await requestClose())) return;
        state.definitionId = '';
        state.statusCode = '';
        setMode('list');
        reload();
    });

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Review (542, folded into 543): Submit for Review / Approve.
    // Same endpoints and body the Audit Definition menu used
    // (POST definitions/{id}/submit | approve). The 537 gate still checks
    // the configuration on the server (THROW 53612).
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function reviewItems(id, statusCode, openSteps) {
        const items = [];
        if (statusCode === 'Draft')
            items.push({ icon: 'fa-paper-plane', label: 'Submit for Review', run: function () { submitForReview(id, openSteps()); } });
        if (statusCode === 'UnderReview')
            items.push({ icon: 'fa-check', label: 'Approve', run: function () { approve(id); } });
        return items;
    }

    async function submitForReview(id, open) {
        if (open && open.length) {
            await box('Complete every step before submitting the audit for review. Not complete: ' + open.join(', ') + '.', 'warning');
            return;
        }
        const reason = await window.gracUi.prompt('Reason (optional):',
            { title: 'Submit for Review', inputLabel: 'Reason', confirmText: 'Submit' });
        if (reason === null) return;   // cancelled
        await transition(id, 'submit', reason, 'Submitted for review.');
    }
    // 544 (sir): approving makes the audit Active at once -- the approve
    // procedure runs Approved and then Active; no separate Activate.
    async function approve(id) {
        const reason = await window.gracUi.prompt('Approving makes the audit Active. Reason (optional):',
            { title: 'Approve and activate', inputLabel: 'Reason', confirmText: 'Approve' });
        if (reason === null) return;
        await transition(id, 'approve', reason, 'Audit approved. It is now Active.');
    }
    async function transition(id, action, reason, done) {
        try {
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/definitions/' + encodeURIComponent(id) + '/' + action), {
                method      : 'POST',
                credentials : 'same-origin',
                headers     : { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
                body        : JSON.stringify({
                    organizationId : Number(state.orgId),
                    definitionId   : Number(id),
                    reasonText     : reason || null,
                    actor          : null
                })
            });
            const j = await r.json().catch(function () { return null; });
            if (!r.ok) { await box('Failed: ' + ((j && (j.error || j.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status)), 'error'); return; }
            await box(done, 'success');
        } catch (err) {
            await box('Failed: ' + (err.message || err), 'error');
            return;
        }
        if (state.mode === 'view' && state.definitionId === String(id)) loadView();
        else if (state.mode === 'audit' && state.definitionId === String(id)) loadAuditView();
        else reload();
    }

    if (window.gracPageActions) {
        window.gracPageActions.attach('oaCfgActionsBtn', function () {
            if (!state.definitionId) return [];
            const id = state.definitionId;
            // The audit view (3-dot View) offers the step list too.
            const head = state.mode === 'audit'
                ? [{ icon: 'fa-pen', label: 'Configure', run: function () { openView(id); } }]
                : [];
            return head.concat(reviewItems(id, state.statusCode, openStepNames));
        });
    }
    el.submit.addEventListener('click', function () { submitForReview(state.definitionId, openStepNames()); });
    el.approve.addEventListener('click', function () { approve(state.definitionId); });

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // List
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // The row's step statuses: no longer columns (sir), still read for the
    // 3-dot Submit for Review, which names the steps not yet complete.
    const LIST_STEPS = [
        ['Scope Builder',    'scopeStatus',           'ScopeStatus'],
        ['Question Sets',    'questionsStatus',       'QuestionsStatus'],
        ['Workflow',         'workflowStatus',        'WorkflowStatus'],
        ['Scoring',          'scoringStatus',         'ScoringStatus']
    ];

    async function reload() {
        if (!state.orgId) {
            el.body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">Select an organization to load audits.</td></tr>';
            wf.updatePager('oa-cfg', { pageNumber: 1, totalCount: 0, pageSize: 1 });
            return;
        }
        el.body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">Loading...</td></tr>';
        try {
            const qs = new URLSearchParams();
            qs.set('organizationId', state.orgId);
            if (state.search) qs.set('search', state.search);
            qs.set('page', String(state.page));
            qs.set('pageSize', String(state.pageSize));
            const r = await fetch(U(API + '/configuration-audits?' + qs.toString()), { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            const body = await r.json().catch(function () { return null; });
            if (!r.ok) throw new Error((body && (body.error || body.Error)) || ('HTTP ' + r.status));
            state.total = Number(pick(body, 'totalCount', 'TotalCount') || 0);
            const rows = pick(body, 'rows', 'Rows') || [];
            renderRows(rows);
            wf.updatePager('oa-cfg', { pageNumber: state.page, totalCount: state.total, pageSize: state.pageSize, rowCount: rows.length });
        } catch (err) {
            el.body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">Failed to load: ' + esc(err.message || err) + '</td></tr>';
        }
    }

    function renderRows(rows) {
        state.rows = {};
        if (!rows.length) {
            el.body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty">No audits to configure. A new audit appears here once its details are saved in Audit Definition.</td></tr>';
            return;
        }
        el.body.innerHTML = rows.map(function (row) {
            const p = function (a, b) { return pick(row, a, b); };
            const id = String(p('definitionId', 'DefinitionId'));
            state.rows[id] = row;
            const owner = wf.personWithRole(p('ownerDisplayName', 'OwnerDisplayName'), p('ownerRoleName', 'OwnerRoleName'));
            const ver = p('currentVersionLabel', 'CurrentVersionLabel') || (p('currentVersionNumber', 'CurrentVersionNumber') ? String(p('currentVersionNumber', 'CurrentVersionNumber')) : '');
            const done = Number(p('configuredSteps', 'ConfiguredSteps') || 0);
            const all  = Number(p('configurationSteps', 'ConfigurationSteps') || 4);
            return '<tr class="pm-row-clickable" data-id="' + esc(id) + '">'
                + '<td>' + esc(p('definitionCode', 'DefinitionCode')) + '</td>'
                + '<td>' + esc(p('definitionName', 'DefinitionName')) + '</td>'
                + '<td>' + esc(owner) + '</td>'
                + '<td>' + esc(ver) + '</td>'
                + '<td>' + esc(p('currentStatusName', 'CurrentStatusName')) + '</td>'
                + '<td>' + esc(done + '/' + all) + '</td>'
                + '<td><button type="button" class="pm-action-trigger" data-id="' + esc(id) + '"'
                + ' aria-haspopup="menu" aria-expanded="false" title="Actions">'
                + '<i class="fas fa-ellipsis-v fa-solid fa-ellipsis-vertical" aria-hidden="true"></i>'
                + '<span class="visually-hidden">Actions</span></button></td>'
                + '</tr>';
        }).join('');

        // 3-dot: View, then Submit for Review / Approve by status.
        if (window.gracPageActions) {
            el.body.querySelectorAll('.pm-action-trigger').forEach(function (btn) {
                const id  = btn.getAttribute('data-id');
                const row = state.rows[id];
                window.gracPageActions.attach(btn, function () {
                    // sir, 2026-11-13: View = the whole audit, read-only (the
                    // Audit Definition view page); Configure = the step list
                    // (also a row click).
                    return [{ icon: 'fa-up-right-from-square', label: 'View', run: function () { openAuditView(id); } },
                            { icon: 'fa-pen', label: 'Configure', run: function () { openView(id); } }]
                        .concat(reviewItems(id, pick(row, 'currentStatusCode', 'CurrentStatusCode') || '', function () {
                            return LIST_STEPS.filter(function (s) { return pick(row, s[1], s[2]) !== 'Completed'; })
                                             .map(function (s) { return s[0]; });
                        }));
                });
            });
        }
    }

    // Row click = View (the Audit Definition list's pattern).
    el.body.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        if (e.target.closest('.pm-action-trigger, a, button, input, label, select')) return;
        const tr = e.target.closest('tr.pm-row-clickable[data-id]');
        if (tr) openView(tr.getAttribute('data-id'));
    });

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // View: facts and the six steps; Configure opens a step under its row.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function fmtDate(v) {
        if (!v) return '';
        if (typeof window.gracFormatDisplayDate === 'function') {
            const g = window.gracFormatDisplayDate(v); if (g !== v) return g;
        }
        return String(v).slice(0, 10);
    }
    function facts(rows) {
        return rows.map(function (r) {
            return '<div><dt>' + esc(r[0]) + '</dt>'
                 + (r[1] ? '<dd>' + esc(r[1]) + '</dd>' : '<dd class="oa-wv-empty">Not set</dd>') + '</div>';
        }).join('');
    }
    function setMessage(text) {
        const m = document.getElementById('oaCfgMessage');
        m.style.display = text ? 'block' : 'none';
        m.style.background = 'var(--danger-100)'; m.style.color = 'var(--danger-700)';
        m.textContent = text || '';
    }

    // The list's 3-dot View (sir): the Audit Definition view page, the whole
    // audit read-only -- js/Shared/audit-view.js, shared with that page.
    async function openAuditView(id) {
        if (!(await requestClose())) return;
        if (String(id || '') !== state.definitionId) { state.name = ''; state.statusCode = ''; state.steps = []; }
        state.definitionId = String(id || '');
        setMode('audit');
        el.heading.textContent  = state.name || 'Audit Configuration';
        el.subtitle.textContent = 'This audit, read-only: its details and its configuration.';
        loadAuditView();
    }
    async function loadAuditView() {
        if (!state.definitionId || !state.orgId) return;
        const msg = document.getElementById('oaCfgAvMessage');
        msg.style.display = 'none'; msg.textContent = '';
        try {
            const d = await window.gracAuditView.render(document.getElementById('oaCfgAvBody'), {
                orgId: state.orgId, definitionId: state.definitionId, chipHtml: chip,
                onSteps: function (steps) { state.steps = steps; }
            });
            if (!d) return;
            state.name = pick(d, 'definitionName', 'DefinitionName') || '';
            state.statusCode = pick(d, 'currentStatusCode', 'CurrentStatusCode') || '';
            el.heading.textContent = state.name || 'Audit Configuration';
            document.getElementById('oaCfgAvStatus').textContent = pick(d, 'currentStatusName', 'CurrentStatusName') || '-';
            const ver = window.gracAuditView.versionLabel(d);
            const verEl = document.getElementById('oaCfgAvVersion');
            verEl.textContent = ver; verEl.hidden = !ver;
        } catch (err) {
            msg.style.display = 'block';
            msg.style.background = 'var(--danger-100)'; msg.style.color = 'var(--danger-700)';
            msg.textContent = 'Could not load this audit: ' + (err.message || err);
        }
    }
    document.getElementById('oaCfgAvRefreshBtn').addEventListener('click', loadAuditView);

    function openView(id) {
        const changed = String(id || '') !== state.definitionId;
        // A different audit never shows the previous one's name or steps.
        if (changed) { state.name = ''; state.statusCode = ''; state.steps = []; }
        state.definitionId = String(id || '');
        setMode('view');
        el.heading.textContent  = state.name || 'Audit Configuration';
        el.subtitle.textContent = 'Use Configure on a step to open it under its row. Each step is saved there.';
        // Bind the hosted step screens to this audit now, so a step opens
        // on loaded data.
        if (window.__oaFlowShell) window.__oaFlowShell.setContext(state.orgId, state.definitionId);
        loadView();
    }

    async function loadView() {
        if (!state.definitionId || !state.orgId) return;
        const id  = encodeURIComponent(state.definitionId);
        const org = encodeURIComponent(state.orgId);
        const get = function (path) {
            return fetch(U(API + path), { credentials: 'same-origin' })
                .then(function (r) { if (!r.ok) throw new Error('HTTP ' + r.status); return r.json(); });
        };
        setMessage('');
        try {
            const res = await Promise.all([
                get('/definitions/' + id + '?organizationId=' + org),
                get('/definitions/' + id + '/setup-status?organizationId=' + org)
            ]);
            const d = res[0] && (res[0].data || res[0].Data);
            if (!d) throw new Error('Audit not found.');
            renderFacts(d);
            renderSteps((res[1] && (res[1].steps || res[1].Steps)) || []);
        } catch (err) {
            setMessage('Could not load this audit: ' + (err.message || err));
        }
    }

    function renderFacts(d) {
        const p = function (a, b) { return pick(d, a, b); };
        state.name = p('definitionName', 'DefinitionName') || '';
        state.statusCode = p('currentStatusCode', 'CurrentStatusCode') || '';
        el.heading.textContent = state.name || 'Audit Configuration';
        el.subtitle.textContent = state.statusCode === 'Draft'
            ? 'Use Configure on a step to open it under its row. Each step is saved there.'
            : 'Read-only: the audit is ' + (p('currentStatusName', 'CurrentStatusName') || state.statusCode) + '. Use View on a step to see it.';
        document.getElementById('oaCfgStatus').textContent = p('currentStatusName', 'CurrentStatusName') || '-';
        const ver = p('currentVersionLabel', 'CurrentVersionLabel') || (p('currentVersionNumber', 'CurrentVersionNumber') ? 'v' + p('currentVersionNumber', 'CurrentVersionNumber') : '');
        const verEl = document.getElementById('oaCfgVersion');
        verEl.textContent = ver; verEl.hidden = !ver;
        document.getElementById('oaCfgFacts').innerHTML = facts([
            ['Code',               p('definitionCode', 'DefinitionCode')],
            ['Name',               p('definitionName', 'DefinitionName')],
            ['Assurance Category', p('assuranceCategoryName', 'AssuranceCategoryName')],
            ['Owner',              wf.personWithRole(p('ownerDisplayName', 'OwnerDisplayName'), p('ownerRoleName', 'OwnerRoleName'))],
            ['Effective Date',     fmtDate(p('effectiveDate', 'EffectiveDate'))],
            ['Status',             p('currentStatusName', 'CurrentStatusName')],
            ['Version',            ver]
        ]);
    }

    function findStep(key) {
        return state.steps.find(function (x) { return pick(x, 'stepKey', 'StepKey') === key; }) || null;
    }
    // 564: an Optional step (Control and Practice Mapping, nothing mapped)
    // is not open -- it never blocks Submit for Review.
    function openStepNames() {
        return state.steps.filter(function (s) {
                              const st = pick(s, 'status', 'Status');
                              return st !== 'Completed' && st !== 'Optional';
                          })
                          .map(function (s) { return pick(s, 'stepName', 'StepName'); });
    }

    // Why a step cannot be opened yet, or '' when it can; and a short line
    // under a step's name when its status needs explaining. 545: the only
    // rules (Scope Resolution needs a saved, unchanged scope) left with
    // that step, so every step opens; the hooks stay for the next rule.
    function blockedReason(key) { return ''; }
    function stepNote(key, status, items) { return ''; }

    function renderSteps(steps) {
        state.steps = steps.filter(function (s) { return pick(s, 'stepKey', 'StepKey') !== 'details'; });
        document.getElementById('oaCfgSteps').innerHTML = state.steps.map(function (s) {
            const key    = pick(s, 'stepKey', 'StepKey');
            const status = pick(s, 'status', 'Status');
            const items  = pick(s, 'itemCount', 'ItemCount');
            const note   = stepNote(key, status, items);
            const blocked = blockedReason(key);
            const label   = state.statusCode === 'Draft' ? 'Configure' : 'View';
            return '<tr data-step="' + esc(key) + '">'
                 + '<td>' + esc(pick(s, 'stepName', 'StepName'))
                 + (note ? '<div class="oa-cfg-step-note">' + esc(note) + '</div>' : '') + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + chip(status) + '</td>'
                 + '<td>' + esc(items) + '</td>'
                 + '<td><button type="button" class="pm-button icon" data-configure="' + esc(key) + '"'
                 + ' aria-expanded="false" title="' + esc(blocked || label) + '" aria-label="' + esc(label + ' ' + pick(s, 'stepName', 'StepName')) + '"'
                 + (blocked ? ' disabled' : '') + '>'
                 + '<i class="fa-solid fa-pen" aria-hidden="true"></i></button></td></tr>';
        }).join('') || '<tr><td colspan="4" class="pm-empty">No status available.</td></tr>';
        // The step list was rebuilt: an open step goes back under its row.
        mountFrame();

        // 542: Submit for Review shows on a Draft, enabled once every step
        // is Completed; Approve shows Under Review.
        const open  = openStepNames();
        const draft = state.statusCode === 'Draft';
        el.submit.hidden   = !draft;
        el.submit.disabled = open.length > 0;
        el.submit.title    = open.length ? 'Not complete: ' + open.join(', ') : '';
        el.approve.hidden  = state.statusCode !== 'UnderReview';
        document.getElementById('oaCfgReady').textContent = !draft
            ? (state.statusCode === 'UnderReview' ? 'Under review. The configuration is read-only.' : '')
            : (open.length
                ? 'Not complete: ' + open.join(', ') + '. The audit can be submitted for review once every step is complete.'
                : 'Configuration complete. Submit the audit for review.');
    }
    document.getElementById('oaCfgViewRefreshBtn').addEventListener('click', loadView);

    // 543 (sir): a step opens from its Configure button only, not a row click.
    document.getElementById('oaCfgSteps').addEventListener('click', function (e) {
        const btn = e.target.closest('button[data-configure]');
        if (!btn || btn.closest('.oa-cfg-expand')) return;
        toggleStep(btn.getAttribute('data-configure'));
    });

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Step row expand (543, sir): the Configure button opens the step's
    // screen in a row under it, the Question Sets grid's expand pattern.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Steps with a Save of their own. msg: the screen's inline message,
    // hidden by [hidden] (byHidden) or by style.display.
    const SAVE = {
        'scope'     : { api: '__oaScopeBuilder',   msg: 'oaScopeMessage', byHidden: true  },
        'mapping'   : { api: '__oaMapping',        msg: 'oaMapMessage',   byHidden: false },   // 564
        'questions' : { api: '__oaAdoption',       msg: 'oaAdoptMessage', byHidden: false },
        'workflow'  : { api: '__oaWorkflowConfig', msg: 'oaWfMessage',    byHidden: true  },
        'scoring'   : { api: '__oaScoringConfig',  msg: 'oaScMessage',    byHidden: true  }
    };
    // A line beside Cancel / Save for steps that need one (the Scope
    // Builder's Preview reads the saved scope).
    const ACT_NOW = {
        'scope'   : 'Save the subjects before Step 2: Discover reads the saved subjects.'   // 562
    };
    // The frame around an open step (caption, the step's panel, Cancel /
    // Save). It and every step panel wait in the hidden holder; the open
    // step's panel goes into the frame and the frame into the expand row.
    const frame = {
        root    : document.getElementById('oaCfgFrame'),
        caption : document.getElementById('oaCfgFrameCaption'),
        body    : document.getElementById('oaCfgFrameBody'),
        hint    : document.getElementById('oaCfgFrameHint'),
        cancel  : document.getElementById('oaCfgFrameCancel'),
        save    : document.getElementById('oaCfgFrameSave')
    };
    const home = {};   // stepKey -> the panel's place in the flow shell
    const pop  = { key: '', panel: null, dirty: false, saving: false };

    function clearStepMessage(key) {
        const cfg  = SAVE[key];
        const node = cfg && document.getElementById(cfg.msg);
        if (!node) return;
        if (cfg.byHidden) node.hidden = true; else node.style.display = 'none';
        node.textContent = '';
    }
    function shownStepMessage(key) {
        const cfg  = SAVE[key];
        const node = cfg && document.getElementById(cfg.msg);
        if (!node) return null;
        const shown = cfg.byHidden ? !node.hidden : node.style.display !== 'none';
        return shown && String(node.textContent || '').trim() ? node : null;
    }

    // Puts the frame in an expand row under the open step's row. Also run
    // after the step list is re-rendered (its rows are rebuilt), so an open
    // step stays open; the frame and panel are kept by reference meanwhile.
    function mountFrame() {
        if (!pop.key) return;
        const body = document.getElementById('oaCfgSteps');
        const row  = body.querySelector('tr[data-step="' + pop.key + '"]');
        if (!row) return;
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        tr.className = 'oa-cfg-expand is-selected';
        const td = document.createElement('td');
        td.colSpan = 4;
        td.appendChild(frame.root);
        tr.appendChild(td);
        row.insertAdjacentElement('afterend', tr);
        // The open step's row stays highlighted while it is open (sir).
        row.classList.add('oa-cfg-step-open', 'is-selected');
        const btn = row.querySelector('[data-configure]');
        if (btn) btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
    }

    // Closes the open step: its panel goes back to the flow shell, the
    // frame back to the holder, the expand row away.
    function unmountStep() {
        if (pop.panel && home[pop.key]) home[pop.key].appendChild(pop.panel);
        document.getElementById('oaCfgHolder').appendChild(frame.root);
        const tr = document.querySelector('#oaCfgSteps tr.oa-cfg-expand');
        if (tr) tr.remove();
        const row = document.querySelector('#oaCfgSteps tr.oa-cfg-step-open');
        if (row) row.classList.remove('oa-cfg-step-open', 'is-selected');
        const btn = document.querySelector('#oaCfgSteps [data-configure][aria-expanded="true"]');
        if (btn) btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
        pop.key = '';
        pop.panel = null;
        pop.dirty = false;
    }

    async function openStep(key) {
        if (!state.definitionId || !key) return;
        const blocked = blockedReason(key);
        if (blocked) { await box(blocked, 'warning'); return; }
        const panel = document.querySelector('#oaCfgHolder [data-flow-panel="' + key + '"]');
        if (!panel) return;

        const editable = state.statusCode === 'Draft';
        const caption  = panel.querySelector(':scope > .oa-ws-section-hint');
        frame.caption.textContent = caption ? caption.textContent : '';
        frame.save.hidden   = !(SAVE[key] && editable);
        frame.save.disabled = false;
        frame.cancel.textContent = SAVE[key] && editable ? 'Cancel' : 'Close';
        frame.hint.textContent = editable ? (ACT_NOW[key] || '') : 'Read-only: the audit is not a Draft.';

        home[key] = home[key] || panel.parentNode;
        frame.body.appendChild(panel);
        pop.key = key;
        pop.panel = panel;
        pop.dirty = false;
        clearStepMessage(key);
        // Re-apply the audit (a no-op once the screen is bound; binds it if
        // its own pickers were still loading when the view opened), then
        // re-read what is saved, so edits thrown away last time are gone.
        if (window.__oaFlowShell) window.__oaFlowShell.setContext(state.orgId, state.definitionId);
        const api = SAVE[key] && window[SAVE[key].api];
        if (api && typeof api.reload === 'function') {
            try { api.reload(); } catch (_) { /* the screen shows its own error */ }
        }
        // The page does not scroll: the step opens downward from its row,
        // where the user clicked (sir).
        mountFrame();
    }

    // Configure button: open the step, or close it when it is the open one.
    // Another step open first asks to close it (when it has changes).
    async function toggleStep(key) {
        if (pop.saving) return;
        const same = pop.key === key;
        if (pop.key && !(await requestClose())) return;
        if (!same) openStep(key);
    }

    // A change the user makes inside the open step -- typing, picking, or a
    // button of the step screen -- makes it "dirty", and closing then asks
    // first. Not counted: Cancel / Save, a message box over it, and change
    // events raised by code (not isTrusted).
    function markDirty(e) {
        if (!e.isTrusted || !pop.key) return;
        const t = e.target;
        if (!t || !t.closest) return;
        if (t.closest('.grac-dialog-overlay, #oaCfgFrameSave, #oaCfgFrameCancel')) return;
        if (e.type === 'click' && !t.closest('button')) return;
        pop.dirty = true;
    }
    frame.root.addEventListener('input',  markDirty, true);
    frame.root.addEventListener('change', markDirty, true);
    frame.root.addEventListener('click',  markDirty, true);

    // Resolves true when the step was closed (or none was open).
    async function requestClose() {
        if (pop.saving) return false;
        if (!pop.key) return true;
        if (pop.dirty && SAVE[pop.key] && state.statusCode === 'Draft') {
            const ok = await window.gracUi.confirm('Close without saving? The changes made here will be lost.',
                { type: 'warning', title: 'Unsaved changes', confirmText: 'Close without saving' });
            if (!ok) return false;
        }
        unmountStep();
        // The scope Preview saves while open: show what is saved.
        loadView();
        return true;
    }
    frame.cancel.addEventListener('click', requestClose);

    async function saveStep() {
        const key = pop.key;
        const cfg = SAVE[key];
        const api = cfg && window[cfg.api];
        if (!api || pop.saving) return;
        pop.saving = true;
        frame.save.disabled = true;
        clearStepMessage(key);
        let ok = false;
        try {
            ok = await api.save();
        } catch (_) {
            ok = false;
        } finally {
            pop.saving = false;
            frame.save.disabled = false;
        }
        if (!ok) {
            // The step screen's own message says why; the step stays open on it.
            const m = shownStepMessage(key);
            if (m) m.scrollIntoView({ block: 'nearest' });
            else await box('Not saved.', 'error');
            return;
        }
        const s = findStep(key);
        const title = (s && pick(s, 'stepName', 'StepName')) || key;
        clearStepMessage(key);
        unmountStep();
        await loadView();
        await box(title + ' saved.', 'success');
    }
    frame.save.addEventListener('click', saveStep);

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Boot
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot);
    if (document.readyState !== 'loading') boot();
    let booted = false;

    async function boot() {
        if (booted) return;
        booted = true;
        setMode('list');

        wf.wirePager('oa-cfg', function (delta) {
            const next = state.page + delta;
            const maxPage = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(state.total / state.pageSize));
            if (next < 1 || next > maxPage) return;
            state.page = next;
            reload();
        });

        const orgs = await wf.loadOrgs();
        if (!orgs.length) {
            el.org.innerHTML = '<option value="">No accessible organizations</option>';
            reload();
            return;
        }
        wf.populateOrgSelect('oaCfgFilterOrganization', orgs);
        state.orgId = el.org.value || '';

        el.org.addEventListener('change', function () {
            state.orgId = el.org.value || '';
            state.page = 1;
            reload();
        });
        document.getElementById('oaCfgSearch').addEventListener('input', function (e) {
            state.search = e.target.value || '';
            state.page = 1;
            clearTimeout(state.searchTimer);
            state.searchTimer = setTimeout(reload, 250);
        });
        document.getElementById('oaCfgRefreshBtn').addEventListener('click', reload);

        // Opened from Audit Definition on one audit (537): the audit and
        // its organization are in the navigation code. 543: straight to its
        // view, the step list; Back goes to the list.
        const ctx = window.gracSecureNav ? await window.gracSecureNav.context('org-audit-configuration') : null;
        if (ctx && ctx.error) {
            reload();
            await box(ctx.error, 'error');
            return;
        }
        if (ctx && ctx.filterType === 'AuditDefinition' && ctx.filterId) {
            const org = ctx.organizationId ? String(ctx.organizationId) : '';
            if (org && Array.prototype.some.call(el.org.options, function (o) { return o.value === org; })) el.org.value = org;
            state.orgId = el.org.value || state.orgId;
            reload();
            openView(String(ctx.filterId));
            return;
        }
        reload();
    }
})();
</script>
